There is another way to quickly acquire alot of stolen goods. The murder 
farm in grahtwood. Have someone murder a ton of npcs and then sneak and 
loot them. No bounty.
----
It's possible to find legendary loot in safeboxes... or at least I found 
The shivering cheese in one in Bal foyen crafting area in an intermediate box.

----
Still: "Best thieves are Khajiit and Wood Elves. Both gain 3 meter 
detection radius decrease with their passive racial abilities" is 
wrong. With U21 (Wrathstone DLC | February 2019) Bosmer's 3m 
detection radius reduction (Stealthy racial passive) was replaced 
with Stealth detection radius by 3m (Hunter Eye racial passive). 
So Wood Elves has lost their detection radius reduction. Patch 
notes (there is also a developers comment on this change): 
https://forums.elderscrollsonline.com/en/discussion/460633/pc-mac-patch-notes-v4-3-5-wrathstone-update-21

Also it worths to note, that pickpocketing might be more profitable, 
as Vvardenfell NPCs have a chance of providing one of 3 houses motif 
pages (which are 5..8K at PC EU) and some specific NPCs have green/blue 
furnishing plans which are available from pickpocketing only.

Again, thank you for the guide. It is great you use your own experience 
and share this.

